        <strong class="cs-panel-title">2. Pain Point: Updating 1 String or Array in Binary Formats (Arrow / FlatBuffers) Forces a Full Buffer Rebuild</strong>
        <p class="cs-sub">
          Immutable columnar/binary buffers (Apache Arrow, FlatBuffers) cannot mutate variable-length strings or arrays without unpacking and rebuilding the entire table. <code>capnstruct</code> stores fixed-size fields in an 8-byte-aligned <code>#[repr(C)]</code> table and variable-length strings/slices in a relative-offset <strong>tail arena</strong> so you can mutate fields directly on the binary view:
        </p>
